SUMMARY:HW: Lion Reflection Questions (P2-Honors Biology-Avery) (0403_1310
 2Y_Honors Biology-0012_2627)
DESCRIPTION:Status: todo\nClass: 0403_13102Y_Honors Biology-0012_2627\nCho
 ose TWO of the four questions to answer based on the documentary series L
 ion.  Your responses should include specific examples from the series and
  make direct connections to what we have learned in class.  Each response
  should be 4-6 sentences in length.  You should use proper grammar\, capi
 talization and punctuation.  This is an individual assignment and the use
  of AI on this assignment in prohibited.  \n\n* Adaptation & Survival\n\n
 The documentary follows lions navigating threats like drought\, prey scar
 city\, and rival prides. What physical and behavioral adaptive traits do 
 lions have that help them survive in their environment\, and how do these
  traits reflect natural selection at work in real time?\n\n* Social Struc
 ture & Evolutionary Advantage\n\nLions are unique among big cats for livi
 ng in social groups. Based on what you observed\, why might group living 
 have evolved as an advantageous strategy for lions specifically\, and wha
 t biological trade-offs (downsides) come with living in close \nhttps://b
 cpss.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course_46327&month=09&year
 =2026#assignment_2423018
URL:https://bcpss.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course_46327&m
 onth=09&year=2026#assignment_2423018
