SUMMARY:HW: 10/01 Activity Theme Park Access (AP Computer Science Principl
 es_SY26-27)
DESCRIPTION:Status: todo\nClass: AP Computer Science Principles_SY26-27\nA
 ctivity -  Theme Part Access\n\nYou will create an app that determines a 
 persons access based on:\n\nHeight → Age → Adult supervision\n\nThen rewr
 ite one nested solution as a compound Boolean expression.\n\nThe planning
  document specifically emphasizes that nested versus compound structures 
 can both be valid designs and students should compare them for readabilit
 y.\n\nYour goal: Create a Python app that decides whether a person can ri
 de an attraction by checking height → age → adult supervision. Then rewri
 te your nested solution using a compound Boolean expression.\n\nRide Rule
 s\n----------\n\nUse these fictional rules for this activity:\n\n*\n\nRid
 ers must be at least 48 inches tall.\n\n*\n\nRiders who meet the height r
 equirement and are 12 or older may ride without an adult.\n\n*\n\nRiders 
 who meet the height requirement but are under 12 need adult supervision.\
 n\nDirections\n----------\n\n*\n\nOpen your Python editor and create a fi
 le named theme_park_access.py.\n\n*\n\nAsk the user to enter their height
  in inches and \nhttps://bcpss.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=
 course_46019&month=10&year=2026#assignment_2433016
URL:https://bcpss.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course_46019&m
 onth=10&year=2026#assignment_2433016
